--
-- Consumed by nvim/.config/nvim/lua/theme/palette.lua, which `dofile`s this
-- exact path (~/.local/state/theme/nvim.lua) fresh on every colorscheme
-- load. ROLES ONLY — twelve Material You role colours, nothing more. This
-- file must NEVER learn what a syntax slot is: nvim/.config/nvim/lua/theme/
-- ramp.lua derives keyword/string/function/etc. from these roles in Lua at
-- load time, because a text template cannot do colour math. Widening this
-- file to carry syntax colours directly would duplicate that logic in a
-- place that cannot compute it.
